And even among those still loyal to Gaia, great rivalries
and grudges ensue, for Garou passions are ever near
the surface, and legendarily volatile. A werewolf may
meet her death not at the claws of a venomous fomor or
in the bowels of a caustic chemical plant, but by losing an
overzealous duel of honor to another werewolf, by spirit
trickery into disadvantage against a duplicitous ally, or
even by betrayal and subsequently being torn to shreds at
a moot. Whenever werewolves meet, despite a high likelihood
of participants “being on the same side,” camaraderie
is far from certain. The possibility of violence always
lurks throughout such an encounter.
For more information on the dangers posed by other
werewolves, see The Shadow of the Past on p. 35.
