When the players’ characters enter the Umbra, they
should immediately have a sense of duality. It is a
place of great power, and the Garou have access to
its spaces, gifts, and wonders. At the same time, it
is a place of terrifying unknowableness, and even
the half-spirit Garou are effectively interlopers in a
world that belongs only partially to them, and partially
eludes them because its truths would sunder their
minds to learn. It is much like the sea, which seems
mysterious and even romantic to humans who don’t
