What they might want: The nethermost strand of the
Weaver’s web, every thought of autumn, a kiss from
Gaia’s lips, the depths of the sea, redemption
IN STORIES
Celestines don’t take direct, personal action; it’s probably
incorrect to think of them as “people” in the context that
most Garou have. If the players’ characters interact with a
Celestine, it’s almost certainly through an avatar or servitor-
spirit pursuing that Celestine’s goals on an individual
level (which means they’re some form of lesser spirit). Celestines
help give context to the story on a thematic level,
or perhaps charge the pack (through intermediary spirits)
with some sort of legendary oath. Often what they desire
is metaphorical, as might be the actions the pack may
take in their name — those exceedingly rare packs in
which a Celestine takes an interest, of course.
