Spider-Shifter
Seething, scuttling, swarming over their prey, the
spider-shifter devours all that stands before it and leaves
only a desiccated husk in its wake, or perhaps a paralyzed
victim left bound in a silken prison. A companion of
shadows, at once alone in its legion, the spider-shifter can
take the form of a single person (often on the margins
of cosmopolitan society) or a swarm of thousands of
web-crawling arachnids. Some werewolves swear that
the spider-shifters can take on a more menacing form as
well…
